    "created_at": "2017-08-16T15:14:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-08-16T15:14:27Z",
    "body": "You quoted a \"should\" requirement, but missed the \"must\" requirement:\r\n\r\n> The addition must have the support of at least two implementers. (Such support is not binding in any way on the implementers, however.) \r\n\r\nSince we have support from zero implementers, this will not be implemented anywhere. As such, we will not include it in the standard. The standard does not include wishful thinking or fiction, but instead features for which it is useful to create an interoperable specification on how to implement.\r\n\r\nClosing, but happy to continue discussing in the closed thread. And, of course, if you manage to get the code added back to 2+ browsers, happy to reopen and reconsider. But until that time, we won't be adding fiction to the HTML Standard.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
